# DVB-T channel rename map - one "raw (tidied) channel name = display name"
# per line, case-insensitive match on the left side. Applied after every
# mapping pass, so it also fixes channels mapped before an entry was added.
# The raw name is what TVHeadend's mapper produces AFTER its own tidying
# (HD/regional suffixes etc already stripped) - check the current name in
# the TVHeadend UI or via GET /dvbt/status if a rename below doesn't match.
#
# CAUTION: pick a target name that doesn't collide with an unrelated
# channel that already has it (e.g. a DVB-T TV regional feed vs. an
# unrelated radio station of a similar name) - the mapper does not merge
# or warn on a collision, it just leaves two channels with the same name.
NDR FS NDS HD = NDR FS Niedersachsen
NDR FS NDS = NDR FS Niedersachsen
